[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1096","stub":{"id":"1096","section":"NC Route 28 to US Route 19","altname":"","river":"Little Tennessee","difficulty":"ItoIIstandoutIII","states":["USA-NCR"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"migration-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"486","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"109307","location":{"latitude":"35.2349014282227","longitude":"-83.3960037231445"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"114549","location":{"latitude":"35.3748016357422","longitude":"-83.5205001831055"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"23","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"101249159","title":null,"post_date":"2012-03-30 04:00:00+00","detail":"Hadn't run this in probably 12 years and discovered that the takeout has changed. Somebody bought the land on river right, put up a bunch of houses, and posted the old trail as \"no trespassing.\" Takeout now is on river left directly under the bridge. It's a way steeper climb, but being right under the bridge, it's more rock and less mud.\n\nAlso, there was a log on river right at the bottom of the Narrows, directly across from the big undercut rock. At 750 cfs, it was just breaking the surface. Not an issue for someone with boat control, but the hole right above there would likely flip a newbie. Scope it out before you take someone through there.","user":{"name":"Sean O'Malley"}},{"id":"100268045","title":null,"post_date":"2008-03-09 05:00:00+00","detail":"At the second bridge over a creek traveling on Needmore Rd., there is a small island on river left. The channel between the island and the bank has a tree strainer blocking the exit from the channel. There is also what appears to be an undercut rock on river right a few minutes down river from this location. The lack of a pillow is very noticeable and it's easy to avoid.","user":{"name":"Roman Ryder"}}],"photos":[{"id":"889805","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"892329","description":"photo taken 8/22/18 at 970 CFS alongside Needmore Rd.","caption":"Little Tennessee","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Harold Johnson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/889805","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/889805"}}],"detail":{"id":"1096","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"Carolina Whitewater, B.Benner\n\nUpper Green and the [Nanty Gorge](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/1101/) (with one exception; see below).\n\nDavid A. DeCoursy wrote:\n\nBeautiful and easy beginner run with close access to NOC. At 950 cfs it's all class I-II with about 4 ledges where you can find some small but suprisingly stronger than expected spots for learning to side-surf and hold your edge. Great for taking newbies for a relaxed introduction to ww kayaking.\n\n\n\nVery pretty, great access for the most part.\n\n\n\nThe end when I went was a very unexpected Class 3 consisting of a breaking wave and hole shortly behind it.\n\n\n\nFontana Lake needs to be low, I've read, or else this last rapid (The Narrows) is under water.\n\n\n\nIn my opinion, for such a simple river, the end is a tad tougher than [Nanty Falls](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/1101/), but without the Class-2 entrance. Scouting will reveal the easily obtained line but when you've been paddling class 1-2 for 6 miles, it IS a suprise. Newbies are bound to flip without a scout. Stay right at the entrance and move to the right of center once past the top breaking wave. You can punch the holes easily at 950 cfs if you're used to such things, but keep in mind the person you are taking may not, especially in light of the relaxed previous miles. (No worries, though; it's all lake after 5 seconds, so it's a very friendly swim.)","averageGradient":"11","maxGradient":"0","length":"22","correlations":[{"reachID":"1096","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"350","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"2000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"LITTLE TENNESSEE RIVER AT NEEDMORE, NC","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"03503000","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"486","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"2.26","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"35.33638889","longitude":"-83.5269444"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/03503000","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/03503000/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"migration-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"486","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["109307","114549"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-83.39598609,35.23577965],[-83.3958988,35.23710853],[-83.39532395,35.23908906],[-83.39596201,35.24204851],[-83.39602781,35.24257818],[-83.39587938,35.24337935],[-83.39528701,35.24486101],[-83.39583095,35.24688314],[-83.39657926,35.24783725],[-83.39696558,35.24810359],[-83.39831445,35.24791231],[-83.40053938,35.24742114],[-83.40334924,35.24731964],[-83.40480076,35.24808326],[-83.4064813,35.24870209],[-83.40999011,35.2491434],[-83.41307762,35.25015874],[-83.41705086,35.24948149],[-83.41840894,35.24966091],[-83.41909974,35.25023643],[-8